description:
Reconcile every user-facing and contributor-facing document with the canonical four-layer contract after the schema, mention migration, and runner settle.

Required corrections include:

- `project/wiki/four-layer-evaluation.md` title and content;
- `tests/eval/ground-truth-schema.md`, including removal of five-grade claims and `conceptId === ruleId`;
- canonical names for mentions, data items, components, flows, capability diagnostics, eligibility reasons, computability states, and baseline readiness;
- removal of `pii_signals`, `pii:`, fuzzy aliases, and legacy identity examples;
- explicit statement that raw hits are diagnostic and no cross-layer scalar exists.

Documentation is generated or contract-tested where possible so schema and prose cannot silently diverge. It lands before legacy compatibility removal.
